scripts/run-smoke-test.ts: FileQueue driver for chart-exemplar 09

scripts/run-smoke-test.ts
- Reads chart-exemplar PNG from disk -> base64
- Configures FileQueueDispatcher (1s poll, 30min per-dispatch timeout,
  cleanup disabled for audit)
- Wraps dispatch() with timing capture for per-agent metrics
- Calls scoreChart() with labeledNqCorpusCount=0 (active /NQ disclaimer
  + score-cap-85)
- On completion writes the full ScoringRun + smoke-test metrics to
  .queue/runs/{runId}.json
- Prints verdict, direction, variant, tier, final score, action params
  (entry/stop/target/R), total dispatches, wall clock, avg per-dispatch

Default exemplar = 09 (NinjaTrader 20-second blue cloud bounce, the
canonical Tier 1 winner). Override with --exemplar=NN.

scripts/fulfill-queue-request.md
- Protocol doc for Claude Code (session driver) describing how to
  fulfill .queue/requests/{id}.json files via Task tool.
- Lists the request schema, the response schema, the recommended
  sub-agent prompt template, and parallelism guidance (Wave 0 + Wave
  A+B+C+D can be fanned out as concurrent Task invocations).

Devdeps added:
- tsx 4.21 — runs TypeScript scripts directly (no separate build step)
- tsconfig-paths 4.2 — resolves @/lib/* aliases for tsx-run scripts

.gitignore: .queue/ already excluded as a runtime artifact dir.

Next: live smoke test execution against chart-exemplar 09. Claude Code
will start the script (background), fulfill ~28 Task dispatches, capture
metrics. Report + halt for user review before authorizing 450-chart
pilot.
